# First-run local setup (ZIP 23111): copy this file to .env.local, then run
# Continental US ZIP entry requires GEOCODIO_API_KEY when NODE_ENV=production
# (Compose `app` service / homelab / next start).
# npm run dev without a key still uses local seed ZIPs for 23111/23116/23223/23231 only.
#
# --- Docker Compose (`docker compose up` / `npm run compose:up`) ---
# The `app` service overrides DATABASE_URL to the internal Compose hostname:
#   postgresql://postgres:postgres@db:5432/yum4less_dev
# (service name `db`, container port 5432 — NOT localhost:5433).
# Host-side npm scripts (`npm run dev`, ingest, Vitest integration) still use
# localhost:5433 below — that publish is loopback-only (SS-1).
# Compose also forces NODE_ENV=production and leaves debug/API-write flags OFF
# (YUM4LESS_DEBUG_ROUTES_ENABLED / YUM4LESS_ENABLE_API_DB_WRITES).
# Optional: place GEOCODIO / Kroger keys in this file; compose loads .env.local
# when present (DATABASE_URL from the compose `environment` block still wins).
# Comma-separated ZIPs for scheduled provider sync / ingest markets (daily cron):
# YUM4LESS_INGEST_ZIPS=23111,30301
# Homelab / Task Scheduler daily cron (from repo root, after .env.local is configured):
#   npm run ingest:weekly-ads:scheduled
# Full Linux homelab runbook: docs/homelab-deploy.md
# Windows Task Scheduler example action:
#   Program: cmd.exe  Arguments: /c cd /d C:\path\to\Yum4Less && npm run ingest:weekly-ads:scheduled
# Linux cron example (03:00 daily):
#   0 3 * * * cd /path/to/Yum4Less && npm run ingest:weekly-ads:scheduled >> /var/log/yum4less-ingest.log 2>&1
# Universal map catalog (OSM Overpass + ranked chain locators) — cron/script primary path:
# npm run ingest:map-catalog
# npm run ingest:map-catalog:fixture   (CI/rehearsal only — requires CI=true or DATABASE_URL_TEST)
# Search-time OSM (read-only API, ephemeral merge when per-chain Postgres pins are sparse): complements daily cron.
# YUM4LESS_MAP_CATALOG_FIXTURE=1
# YUM4LESS_MAP_CATALOG_RADIUS_MILES=12
# YUM4LESS_MAP_OSM_RANKED_CHAIN_POLICY=suppress-conflicts
#   suppress-conflicts (default): OSM gap-fill only; drop OSM Kroger/Aldi when ingested catalog covers chain
#   gap-fill-only: sparse threshold only (no ranked-chain conflict filter)
#   allow-conflicts: legacy merge (dev tuning)
#   off: skip search-time OSM entirely
# YUM4LESS_MAP_SEARCH_OSM_CACHE_TTL_MS=86400000
# Phase C location witness thresholds (ranked-store ingest only):
# YUM4LESS_LOCATION_WITNESS_AGREEMENT_METERS=250
# YUM4LESS_LOCATION_CHANGE_THRESHOLD_METERS=50
# Option A store identity (alias graph) — Slice 2 rank/pantry expand + Slice 3
# Settings canonicalize wired behind the master flag (still default OFF everywhere).
# Client Settings remapping also honors NEXT_PUBLIC_YUM4LESS_STORE_IDENTITY_EXPAND
# (Next.js only inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* into the browser bundle).
# Do not enable in local/dev for shopper paths yet (map/market-search/ingest still exact-id).
# YUM4LESS_STORE_IDENTITY_EXPAND=1
# NEXT_PUBLIC_YUM4LESS_STORE_IDENTITY_EXPAND=1
# YUM4LESS_STORE_IDENTITY_AUTO_CONFIRM=1
# YUM4LESS_STORE_IDENTITY_SNAP_MATCHING=1
# YUM4LESS_STORE_IDENTITY_SEARCH_PROVISIONAL=1
# Wave 2 Part 2 Q2=2A: keep SEARCH_PROVISIONAL OFF unused — ephemeral search pins
# stay permanently excluded from identity/reconciliation (no provisional shopper tier).
# Onboarding: docs/store-identity-source-onboarding.md (three-layer model Q3=3B; Publix Q1=1B).
# Structural note: no-pointer perfect twins score exactly confirmThreshold (0.85);
# Kroger Mechanicsville link is migration-seeded (022), not auto-confirm.
# USDA SNAP map-context reference (batch ingest; not live on user search):
# YUM4LESS_MAP_SNAP_CONTEXT=1
# YUM4LESS_SNAP_CSV_PATH=C:\path\to\store_locations.csv
# YUM4LESS_SNAP_SNAPSHOT_DATE=2025-12-31
# Auto-load SNAP rows when table is empty (npm run dev, setup:local, scheduled ingest, ensure-test-db):
# enabled by default when YUM4LESS_MAP_SNAP_CONTEXT=1 — skips if rows already exist
# YUM4LESS_SNAP_AUTO_ENSURE=0
# YUM4LESS_SNAP_DEV_FIXTURE=1   (ZIP 23111 fixture only — fast local dev instead of full CSV)
# YUM4LESS_SNAP_ENSURE=force     (re-ingest even when rows exist; or: npm run ensure:snap-context -- --force)
# npm run ingest:snap-retailers:fixture   (CI/rehearsal)
# npm run ensure:snap-context   (manual idempotent check)
# Optional Nominatim user agent for coordinate sanity audits (include a real contact method):
# YUM4LESS_NOMINATIM_USER_AGENT=Yum4Less/1.0 (contact: you@example.com)
# YUM4LESS_OSM_OVERPASS_URL=https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter
# Optional tuning when Overpass is slow (respect 1 req/s; cron/script only):
# YUM4LESS_OSM_OVERPASS_TIMEOUT_MS=45000
# YUM4LESS_OSM_OVERPASS_QUERY_TIMEOUT_S=35
# YUM4LESS_OSM_OVERPASS_MAX_ATTEMPTS=2
# YUM4LESS_OSM_OVERPASS_ENDPOINT_BACKOFF_MS=2000
# Fallback tried automatically on HTTP 406/429/5xx: https://overpass.kumi.systems/api/interpreter
# Ranked price reads use a 24-hour cache window; refresh via daily ingest:weekly-ads:scheduled (not user search).
# Scheduled pipeline ends with npm run check:ranked-price-freshness (fail closed on 0 fresh ranked rows in 24h).
# Optional single-operator webhook when that check fails (native fetch — no SaaS):
# YUM4LESS_FRESHNESS_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.example.local/yum4less-freshness
# Emergency escape only (do not leave set on the homelab box):
# YUM4LESS_SKIP_FRESHNESS_HEARTBEAT=1
# Homelab ingest container (Dockerfile.ingest / TrueNAS §10): talk to Postgres over TCP via
# host `psql` instead of `docker exec yum4less-postgres`. Image default is 1.
# YUM4LESS_EXTERNAL_POSTGRES=1
# One-shot dry-run inside the ingest image (exit after one scheduled run):
# YUM4LESS_INGEST_ONCE=1
# Disable in-container cron and keep the container up for host `docker exec` scheduling:
# YUM4LESS_INGEST_CRON=0
# YUM4LESS_PROVIDER_SYNC_ZIP=23111
# Live daily ingest (owner path): npm run setup:local  (requires GEOCODIO + Kroger keys below)
# CI/rehearsal only: npm run ingest:weekly-ads:fixture
GEOCODIO_API_KEY=
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/yum4less_dev
# Dedicated Postgres for fixture/rehearsal ingest (must match DATABASE_URL when running fixture scripts locally):
# DATABASE_URL_TEST=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/yum4less_test
# Public API routes stay read-only by default. Set to 1 only for local dev when you
# want recommendation/market-search calls to persist provider snapshots and sync prices.
# NEVER set in production — NODE_ENV=production ignores this flag; use ingest scripts instead.
# YUM4LESS_ENABLE_API_DB_WRITES=1
# Set to 1 only when a trusted reverse proxy strips client X-Forwarded-For and sets the real IP.
# Without this, rate limits bucket all clients as "unknown" (safer than trusting spoofed headers).
# Prefer platform or Redis-backed limits for multi-instance production deploys.
# TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS=1
# Set to 1 only if TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS=1 is used behind a verified trusted proxy; otherwise a startup warning will fire.
# YUM4LESS_TRUSTED_PROXY_VERIFIED=1
# Enables GET /api/debug/pipeline; leave unset or 0 in production (always 404 there).
# Prefer binding the app to localhost when this is on — do not LAN-expose debug dumps.
# YUM4LESS_DEBUG_ROUTES_ENABLED=1
# Required when debug routes are enabled; without it the route returns 401 (Bearer or X-Yum4Less-Admin-Key).
# YUM4LESS_DEBUG_ADMIN_KEY=
# Privacy-safe first-party analytics is off by default. Local: use memory/stdout.
# Deployed: use postgres only after `db/init/006_analytics_events.sql` is applied
# and a retention/purge policy is documented.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_YUM4LESS_ANALYTICS=1
# YUM4LESS_ENABLE_ANALYTICS=1
# YUM4LESS_ANALYTICS_SINK=memory
# Anonymous customer feedback (complaints, wrong-price reports) — separate from analytics.
# Requires db/init/007_customer_feedback.sql and DATABASE_URL.
# Local dev auto-enables when DATABASE_URL is set; use an explicit flag to override:
# YUM4LESS_FEEDBACK_ENABLED=1
# YUM4LESS_FEEDBACK_ENABLED=0
# Required to authenticate GET /api/feedback when YUM4LESS_FEEDBACK_ENABLED=1; without it the route returns 401 (Bearer or X-Yum4Less-Admin-Key).
# YUM4LESS_FEEDBACK_ADMIN_KEY=
KROGER_CLIENT_ID=
KROGER_CLIENT_SECRET=
# production (intended path after Kroger portal promotion) or certification for new dev apps
KROGER_API_ENV=production
# After Kroger approves production promotion, set credentials above and:
# 1) KROGER_API_ENV=production  (api.kroger.com — store-specific prices)
# 2) npm run probe:kroger-api — confirm Store pricing available: true and item.price.regular/promo
# Certification (api-ce.kroger.com) supports OAuth and catalog only; omit store prices.
# Optional override when you already know the store locationId from the Location API
# Example for ZIP 23111 (Mechanicsville area): 02900529
# KROGER_LOCATION_ID=
# Kroger Location API search limit for map-catalog / provider sync (default 25, max 50)
# YUM4LESS_KROGER_LOCATION_SEARCH_LIMIT=25
# Publix has no direct developer API. Optional third-party product/weekly-ad data via Apify:
# APIFY_API_TOKEN=
# Apify actor (research default): outstanding_vegetable/publix-scraper
# Publix website store-locator only (no token required):
# PUBLIX_STORE_NUMBER=1626
# PUBLIX_STORE_NAME=Brandy Creek Commons
# PUBLIX_STORE_SHORT_NAME=Brandy Creek Comm
# PUBLIX_STORE_OPTION=ACFHLNOTY
WALMART_CLIENT_ID=
WALMART_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional store context for Walmart weekly-ad provenance URLs
# WALMART_STORE_ID=
# Walmart credentials are scaffold-only until an approved official API path is wired.

# MCP (Cursor): copy `.cursor/mcp.json.example` → `.cursor/mcp.json` (gitignored).
# GitHub MCP launcher: `.cursor/hooks/github-mcp.ps1` (Docker stdio).
# Token resolution: GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN if set, else `gh auth token` after `gh auth login`.
# Never commit tokens into `.cursor/mcp.json`. Reload MCP / restart Cursor after changing mcp.json.
# Optional explicit PAT (user env or shell) when you do not want to rely on gh:
GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Weekly-ad ingest (scripts only; not loaded by Next.js for normal app requests)
# Scopes to stores within YUM4LESS_PROVIDER_SYNC_RADIUS_MILES (default 8) of each
# YUM4LESS_INGEST_ZIPS market — same ZIP list as map catalog / scheduled ingest.
# Owner daily path: npm run ingest:weekly-ads:scheduled  (live; requires keys below)
# CI/rehearsal only (deterministic; not daily dev): npm run ingest:weekly-ads:fixture
# Local fixture ingest: set DATABASE_URL_TEST and point DATABASE_URL at the same test database.
# Optional live probes (network; not CI gates):
# npm run probe:kroger-api
# npm run probe:publix-api
# npm run probe:kroger-live-scrape
# npm run probe:publix-live-scrape
# npm run probe:walmart-live-scrape
# Kroger uses browser-first fetch + chain parser; set capture mode while developing parsers
# YUM4LESS_WEEKLY_AD_FIXTURE=1
# YUM4LESS_WEEKLY_AD_BROWSER=1
# YUM4LESS_WEEKLY_AD_NO_BROWSER=1
# YUM4LESS_WEEKLY_AD_CAPTURE=1
# Retry transient Flipp/HTTP scrape failures (429, 5xx, network errors).
# YUM4LESS_WEEKLY_AD_HTTP_RETRIES=3
# YUM4LESS_WEEKLY_AD_BACKOFF_MS=1000
# Provider price sync defaults to ZIP 23111 and radius 8 miles.
# YUM4LESS_PROVIDER_SYNC_ZIP=23111
# YUM4LESS_PROVIDER_SYNC_RADIUS_MILES=8
# Kroger preview/sync stdout diagnostics (default off): YUM4LESS_DEBUG_PROVIDER=1
# Per-ingredient Kroger match scoring logs: YUM4LESS_PROVIDER_MATCH_DEBUG=1
# PowerShell: $env:YUM4LESS_WEEKLY_AD_CAPTURE="1" (not `set`)

# Dev/debug only: show "Project & data details (internal)" link in the meal planner UI
# NEXT_PUBLIC_YUM4LESS_SHOW_INTERNAL_DETAILS=1

# External recipe APIs (research only — not wired to /api/recommendations or user search)
# Dev/test key only; public app-store release needs Patreon supporter key + attribution.
THEMEALDB_API_KEY=1
# Optional cap for sale-driven import runs (default 15 new recipes per run).
# THEMEALDB_IMPORT_MAX_PER_RUN=15
# Opt-in ranking may refresh stale TheMealDB imports on search only when
# YUM4LESS_ENABLE_API_DB_WRITES=1 in local dev (never production HTTP writes).
# Production: use npm run ingest:themealdb:from-sales on your cron host.
# YUM4LESS_ENABLE_THEMEALDB_SEARCH_IMPORT=1
# YUM4LESS_ENABLE_THEMEALDB_SEARCH_IMPORT=0
# Smaller cap for search-path refresh (default 5).
# THEMEALDB_SEARCH_IMPORT_MAX_PER_RUN=5
# Opt-in: run sale-driven TheMealDB import after weekly-ad ingest script completes.
# THEMEALDB_IMPORT_AFTER_WEEKLY_AD=1
# SPOONACULAR_API_KEY=
# EDAMAM_APP_ID=
# EDAMAM_APP_KEY=
